  "scope": "One-player Steel and Cedar full five-battle native Ares review, current retained/indexed forest versus pre-block mixed-forest renderer. Identical read-only VI observer; no marker drawing, per-frame serial logging or added GPU fences. Normal runtime builds remain uninstrumented.",
  "method": {
    "observer": "Track actual VI_ORIGIN framebuffer changes in a vblank callback. Associate each buffer with the stage and context captured by its ordinary 2D callback. Accumulate closed presentation intervals in bounded histograms. Report once after the existing final post-campaign sample, when all active buffers have naturally retired.",
    "boundaries": "Only consecutive active battle buffers from the same stage contribute, excluding loading/story boundaries. Contexts overlap: all is the unique interval total. Dialogue and menu subsets distinguish UI work; settled means no overview/camera/unit/combat motion, so it can also include dialogue/menu.",
    "timing": "FPS is normalized to 60 VI interrupts/second from actual held-VI counts, matching the nominal 30 fps target at 2 VIs/frame. Raw timestamps are also preserved. This is emulator evidence, not a hardware benchmark or guarantee for other modes/projects.",
    "integrity": "Both observers report zero unmapped active origins. Exactly matching presentation-interval counts and final simulation hashes; all histogram bins sum to interval and total-VI counts. Assets and staged filesystem bytes match between variants.",
