  "findings": [
    "Indexed forest commands eliminate every 4-VI hold on Watch, Village and Keep in this run; all four later stages hold every frame for 2 VIs.",
    "Bell improves 24.90 to 26.32 nominal FPS but still has 97 double-length holds in 694 intervals. It remains below target.",
    "Bell dialogue remains a worthwhile UI target: 159 intervals contain 28 four-VI holds (~25.50 nominal FPS); it is not merely a camera-update measurement artifact.",
    "The prior post-campaign 30 fps sample hid active-scene losses; actual presentation evidence now supports the forest optimization without equating before-pacing interval variance to displayed hitches."
  ],
  "validation": "Both complete five-battle native reviews pass with 287 accepted commands, 165 enemy commands, 18 revealed castle cells and canonical hash 600017321675168062 in base 4 MiB. No gameplay, campaign, controller, text, thresholds or artwork changed."
